Building upon previous work by \cite{Ferrara:1971vh}, \cite{Ferrara:1973vz}, we develop a comprehensive integral representation of conformal block operators in CFT$_2$, specifically tailored for spinning primary fields. Notably, this integral expression can be re-expressed as a product of two weighted AdS$_2$ field combinations when the primary fields in question are conserved, which results in the representation of conserved current conformal block operators in CFT$_2$ in terms of geodesic operators defined within the AdS$_2$ framework rather than the AdS$_3$ framework. Moreover, this new perspective enables a direct link between the AdS$_2$ geodesic operator representation and massless higher-spin fields in the AdS$_3$ framework, facilitated by the HKLL bulk field reconstruction method. By harnessing this new picture, we are able to derive a closed-form expression for the four-point conformal block involving spinning primary fields as a product of two AdS$_2$ geodesic Witten diagrams. Additionally, this expression is shown to capture the massless higher-spin dynamics in the AdS$_3$ framework for certain specific combinations of spin. Nevertheless, with increasing spin, the representation on the AdS$_2$ geodesic Witten diagram diagram actually reveals an infinite number of additional operators beyond just the massless higher-spin fields in the AdS$_3$ framework. Consequently, we conclude that the AdS$_2$ geodesic Witten diagram has a more fundamental understanding of the spectrum of the massless higher-spin fields in the AdS$_3$ framework, but also encompasses an infinite number of additional operators for each spin value. Moreover, this new perspective also enables a deeper analysis of the spin spin symmetry in the AdS$_2$ framework, which highlights the presence of an infinite number of higher-spin symmetries in the AdS$_2$ framework, all of which originate from a single AdS$_3$ massless higher-spin field with an infinite number of additional operators for each spin value. Finally, we propose that the AdS$_2$ geodesic Witten diagram may serve as an appropriate effective action framework for the study of massless higher-spin fields in the AdS$_3$ framework. 

